controversy-and-consensus-5 = unlines (cons "One correction on the word *controversy*: *controversia* is Latin (*contrā* + *versus*, from *vertere*), not Greek. The Greek practice it corresponds to is dialectic (*dialegesthai*, to talk through) and *antilogia*, setting argument against argument. That's the method of the Socratic dialogues: one question turned between two speakers until it shows itself. Either way, the classical sense of controversy is the one Avik means: dialogue, turns with polarity." nil)
